1
00:00:00,106 --> 00:00:01,798
(Q31) Good morning everyone.

2
00:00:01,798 --> 00:00:12,551
Now whether you're going to university to study business or some other subject, many of you will eventually end up working for a company of some kind.

3
00:00:12,551 --> 00:00:19,910
Now, when you first start working somewhere you will realise that the organisation you've joined has certain characteristics.

4
00:00:19,910 --> 00:00:32,519
And we often refer to these social characteristics as the culture of the organisation-this includes its unwritten ideas, beliefs, values and things like that.

5
00:00:32,519 --> 00:00:39,806
One well known writer has classified company cultures by identifying four major types.

6
00:00:39,806 --> 00:00:46,802
The first type is called the Power Culture, and it's usually found in small organisations.

7
00:00:46,802 --> 00:00:59,027
[Q31答案句] It's the type of culture that needs a central source of power to be effective, and because control is in the hands of just one or two people there aren't many rules or procedures.

8
00:00:59,027 --> 00:01:09,452
(Q32) [Q32答案句] Another characteristic is that communication usually takes the form of conversations rather than, say, formal meetings or written memos.

9
00:01:09,452 --> 00:01:22,170
(Q33) Now one of the benefits of this culture is that the organisation has the ability to act quickly, so it responds well to threat, or danger on the one hand, and opportunity on the other.

10
00:01:22,170 --> 00:01:27,608
[Q33答案句] But on the negative side, this type of organisation doesn't always act effectively,&nbsp;

11
00:01:27,608 --> 00:01:37,572
because it depends too much on one or two people at the top, and when these people make poor decisions there's no-one else who can influence them.

12
00:01:37,572 --> 00:01:47,564
(Q34) [Q34答案句] And the kind of person who does well in this type of business culture is one who is happy to take risks, and for whom job security is a low priority.

13
00:01:47,564 --> 00:02:01,739
(Q35) [Q35答案句] The next type is known as Role Culture-that's R-O-L-E, not R-O-double L, by the way, and this type is uaually found in large companies, which have lots of different levels in them.

14
00:02:01,739 --> 00:02:10,778
(Q36) These organisations usually have separate departments that specialise in things like finance, or sales, or maintenance, or whatever.

15
00:02:10,778 --> 00:02:16,423
Each one is co-ordinated at the top by a small group of senior managers,&nbsp;

16
00:02:16,423 --> 00:02:28,052
[Q36答案句] and typically everyone's job is controlled by sets of rules and procedures - for example, there are specific job descriptions, rules for discipline, and so on.

17
00:02:28,052 --> 00:02:31,060
(Q37) What are the benefits of this kind of culture?

18
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:43,376
Well firstly, because it's found in large organisations, its fixed costs or over head as they are known are low in the relation to its outputs or what it produces.

19
00:02:43,376 --> 00:02:47,566
In other words it can achieve economies of scale.

20
00:02:47,566 --> 00:02:55,506
[Q37答案句] And secondly, it is particularly successful in business markets where technical expertise is important.

21
00:02:55,506 --> 00:03:03,592
(Q38) [Q38答案句] On the other hand, this culture is often very slow to recognise the need forchange, and even slower to react.

22
00:03:03,592 --> 00:03:06,829
(Q39) What kind of person does this type of culture suit?

23
00:03:06,829 --> 00:03:14,159
[Q39答案句] Well it suits employees who value security, and who don't particularly want to have responsibility.

24
00:03:14,159 --> 00:03:21,983
(Q40) Moving on now to Task Cultures-this type is found in organistations that are project-oriented.

25
00:03:21,983 --> 00:03:30,528
You usually find it where the market for the company's product is extremely competitive or where the products themselves have a short life-span.

26
00:03:30,528 --> 00:03:36,361
Usually top management delegates the projects, the people and other resources.

27
00:03:36,361 --> 00:03:45,937
And once these have been allocated, little day-to-day control is exercised from the top, because this would seem like 'breaking the rules'.

28
00:03:45,937 --> 00:03:50,121
[Q40答案句] Now one of the major benefits of this culture is that it's flexible.

29
00:03:50,121 --> 00:03:53,491
But it does have some major disadvantages too.

30
00:03:53,491 --> 00:03:59,785
For instance, it can't produce economies of scale or great depth of expertise.

31
00:03:59,785 --> 00:04:05,266
People who like working in groups or teams prefer this type of culture.

32
00:04:05,266 --> 00:04:07,766
And finally, the fourth category is called the Person Culture…

